  "raw_reviews": [
    {
      "reviewbody": "This is one of the all time most powerful Grateful Dead shows ever played and simply a MUST HEAR. It is also one of the most enjoyable audience recordings on the entire Archive to listen to. \nA legendary performance to be treasured.",
      "reviewtitle": "One Of The All Time Best",
      "reviewer": "jerkwaterdan",
      "reviewdate": "2008-04-09 09:40:01",
      "createdate": "2008-04-09 09:40:01",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "Finally a better (even if not perfect) recording of one of the best nites of music this planet has ever heard.  This is one to save for those times when you're ready to have your head blown off and can boogie down to your heart's content!  \n\nEnjoy kids!",
      "reviewtitle": "Thank you! Thank you! Thank you!",
      "reviewer": "Cucamunga007",
      "reviewdate": "2008-04-09 19:17:47",
      "createdate": "2008-04-09 19:17:47",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "Ahhhh....this is great...thank you archive & everyone involved for restoring and sharing this show...perfect early Dead at their very best...dream set list and everything!!",
      "reviewtitle": "oh boy!",
      "reviewer": "magicastles",
      "reviewdate": "2008-05-21 04:13:49",
      "createdate": "2008-05-21 04:13:49",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "\"when ken was out, mark & an instigating friend went armed with sony tc d5m's and recorded as much from the masters as they could get away with...\"\n\n^^that's fucked up.",
      "reviewtitle": "really?",
      "reviewer": "najavo",
      "reviewdate": "2008-06-13 12:27:59",
      "createdate": "2008-06-13 12:27:59",
      "stars": "0"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "I first heard a recording of this show in 1987 at a party in Waltham Ma. the night before a Dylan/Dead show at Foxboro Stadium... Blew my mind!!! I got a copy that night and ever since then this was known to my circle as \"The Magic Tape.\" It has been a worthy Guide on many adventurous nights.",
      "reviewtitle": "Magic",
      "reviewer": "elfspice",
      "reviewdate": "2008-08-06 02:01:53",
      "createdate": "2008-08-06 02:01:53",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "They were completely justified in copying the masters..actually they should got him away for a weekend or a week, as long as it took to copy everything..remember, hoarders suck!",
      "reviewtitle": "Ken did the right thing!",
      "reviewer": "lovehaight",
      "reviewdate": "2008-09-01 11:24:02",
      "createdate": "2008-09-01 11:24:02",
      "stars": "3"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "NFA to start the show. The boys must have been rarer to go. I liked the story behind the tape of the show. Mighty Pen shouting it out to all to hear. Not as good as some of the shows I am familiar with but that is the reason why we are not all on the same page anyway. For a real blast check out that KSAN radio show with JG and PL commenting on the songs.",
      "reviewtitle": "Not there",
      "reviewer": "kboyxxx",
      "reviewdate": "2009-01-14 14:08:37",
      "createdate": "2009-01-14 14:08:37",
      "stars": "3"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "These early transitions are beautiful, the dark start jam leading into sugar magnolia is flawless, pure as the driven snow. Paints pictures for what's to come in the years ahead",
      "reviewtitle": "Sick Dark Star",
      "reviewer": "cwswiha07",
      "reviewdate": "2009-02-09 03:32:22",
      "createdate": "2009-02-09 03:32:22",
      "stars": "4"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "Incredible. Just listen to the way Jerry, Bob, and Phil chase each other around during NFA. The seamless transitions. The lock on the drums. Wow.",
      "reviewtitle": "Wow.",
      "reviewer": "shipofthesun",
      "reviewdate": "2009-02-15 05:05:32",
      "createdate": "2009-02-15 03:50:27",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "This is a fantastic set; and it's worth noting that the Grateful Dead shared the bill at the Capitol this night with the New Riders of the Purple Sage--and their tape is extant as well:\nhttp://www.archive.org/details/nrps1970-06-24.weiner.25866.sbeok.shnf\n...taken together, a fabulous document. What a joy it must have been to see them all together!",
      "reviewtitle": "Great show - and not the only one from that night...",
      "reviewer": "koeselitz",
      "reviewdate": "2009-05-17 16:51:36",
      "createdate": "2009-05-17 16:51:36",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "WOW.  This is the best copy of this show I've ever heard.  What a gift.  Thank you Jim and Mark...and the scroogy Ken for recording.  This show changed my life in 1984.  Transcendent.",
      "reviewtitle": "Best recording of this show!",
      "reviewer": "jamiejoon",
      "reviewdate": "2009-10-11 06:34:59",
      "createdate": "2009-10-11 06:34:59",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "bout good old Grateful Dead music can be found in this recording. Pure magic.",
      "reviewtitle": "All that is holy....",
      "reviewer": "Smerdyakov",
      "reviewdate": "2010-02-21 20:10:24",
      "createdate": "2010-02-21 20:10:24",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "What is this foolish ratings system ?\n\nOlympian",
      "reviewtitle": "Thank-you Thank-you, Thank-you Ken",
      "reviewer": "micah6vs8",
      "reviewdate": "2010-06-24 04:22:39",
      "createdate": "2010-06-24 04:22:39",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "Thanks for making this available. What a great back story of how this tape came to be. Love the Dark Star weaving in and out and one of my favourite NFA. Always love an Attics as well. \n\nBe aware though that the archive has complete versions of this show including the spirited UJB and a Swing Low Sweet Chariot with NRPS that end the show. Well worth hearing",
      "reviewtitle": "Fantastic",
      "reviewer": "Pangolin22",
      "reviewdate": "2011-02-21 04:08:29",
      "createdate": "2011-02-21 04:08:29",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "So I've been seeing the dead and listening to shows for 35 years, and I NEVER REALIZED HOW FREAKING INCREDIBLE THEY WERE TILL NOW.  Seriously, this show blows your mind, god how I wish there was a time machine back to 1970.  This takes the Grateful Dead to another level.  Sit back and enjoy, don't gripe about the quality, listen to the brilliance.",
      "reviewtitle": "omfg",
      "reviewer": "CosmicCharlie61",
      "reviewdate": "2012-05-02 20:41:08",
      "createdate": "2012-05-02 20:41:08",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "This is really where it's at. \nThe DS-Attics-DS-SM-DS-SS-CCS-IKR.\n\nWish there was a clear copy of this show, though the AUD used in this version is not bad at all, this is the best source I have heard so far. The Audience doesn't distract from the music, though you can tell how amazed and excited they were. The show gets five stars. the recording gets three stars, but compared to other AUDS is not bad.",
      "reviewtitle": "Wow",
      "reviewer": "MR.SUNSHINE",
      "reviewdate": "2014-06-25 16:56:23",
      "createdate": "2014-06-25 16:56:23",
      "stars": "4"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "...for a good soundboard mix of this one, & let's throw in 3/21/70 while we're at it . I am happy to have this aud, & it's \nactually pretty decent, & has that certain vibe you can't get from a soundboard. This is some very intense, gut-wrenching\npsychedelic blues! Jerry & the boys are channeling another\nworld & bringing it back to us in spades!!!",
      "reviewtitle": "I cut off my right arm...",
      "reviewer": "daskitten",
      "reviewer_itemname": "@daskitten",
      "reviewdate": "2018-10-31 01:47:15",
      "createdate": "2018-10-31 01:47:15",
      "stars": "5"
    },
    {
      "reviewtitle": "In formless reflections of matter",
      "reviewbody": "This show is way ahead of its time.\nThe transitions here are mind blowing!\nBesides a busted string\nand the drop in to Sugar Magnolia \nthat never clicks\nthis is an over the top\nonce in a lifetime show.\nthe entire Dark  \ud83d\udcab \nespecially the segue into Attics\ud83c\udf86\nThis recording captured the delirious rush \nof the Port Chester crowd.\nAs the band weaves in and out of \ud83d\udcab \nWhen they drop into STEPHEN\nand the taper recognizes it\ud83d\ude1b\nAnd really that is what this set is\nRight from Jump\nThe NFA is dripping \nPig nails the Easy Wind\nWith Garcia \ud83c\udfb8 at break neck speed.\nThe Me  & My Uncle \nfinds Weir at the height of\nof his outlaw cowboy self\n\u201cI left his dead ass\nThere by the side of the road\u201d\nCan\u2019t forget this Dark \u26a1\ufe0fevening\nClosing with a \ud83d\udc31-) Rider\n\n\n ",
      "stars": "4",
      "reviewer": "c-freedom",
      "reviewdate": "2025-06-27 13:09:38",
      "createdate": "2025-06-27 13:09:38",
      "reviewer_itemname": "@c-freedom"
    }
